	(text "MCU: RP2040 + W25Q16JVSSIQ QSPI flash, 12 MHz crystal (ABM8-272-T3, 10 pF load: 2x15 pF, 1k series on XOUT, per RP2040 Hardware Design guide 2.3)\nPower: 100 nF per IOVDD pin (C12-C17), USB_VDD (C18), ADC_AVDD (C19); VREG_VIN 1 uF (C20); VREG_VOUT 1 uF (C21) -> DVDD (100 nF C22,C23). Single +3V3 rail, VREG makes 1.1 V.\nUSB-C (J2): 27 R series on D+/D- (R11,R12), 5.1k CC pull-downs (R13,R14). VBUS is NOT connected to +3V3: the board must be powered from J1 (5-32 V) while programming over USB.\nBOOTSEL: SW1 pulls QSPI_SS to GND via 1k (R15) at reset. RESET: SW2 pulls RUN to GND. SWD header J3: 1=SWCLK 2=GND 3=SWDIO (Pico debug-probe order).\nGPIO map: GP0 UART0 TX | GP1 UART0 RX (RS-232) | GP2 CTS | GP3 RTS | GP4 RS485_DIR (DE/RE) | GP5 MODE_SEL (0=RS-232, 1=RS-485)\n GP6 MODE_RB (mode read-back from isolated side) | GP7 LED_STATUS | GP8 LED_ERR | GP13 UART0 RX alt (RS-485 receiver)\n GP16 W5500 MISO | GP17 CS | GP18 SCK | GP19 MOSI | GP20 W5500 RST | GP21 W5500 INT (SPI0, WIZnet-Pico pinout). Unused GPIOs carry no-connect flags.\nFirmware selects the UART0 RX pin (GP1 in RS-232 mode, GP13 in RS-485 mode) according to MODE_SEL."
		(at 20 14 0)
